From: "Claude (SGR dev session)" <claude@sgr-dev.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test(saas): cover routers (auth/apikey/billing) (53% ->
 100%)

- Add tests/saas/test_routers.py: 20 tests covering
  sgr/saas/routers.py's auth_router, apikey_router, billing_router.
- Each router is tested on its own minimal FastAPI app via TestClient
  (no full lifespan needed, same reasoning as tests/api/test_main.py).
  require_auth is overridden via app.dependency_overrides with a
  fixed TokenData where the test targets router logic rather than
  auth itself; one dedicated test confirms require_auth is still
  enforced when NOT overridden (401 without a token).
- Module-level AuthService (_auth) and PerformanceFeeEngine
  (_fee_engine) instances, plus DB session/repository access, are
  patched with AsyncMock/MagicMock doubles, matching the pattern
  established in tests/saas/test_auth.py.
- Covers: register (paper/live rejection, success, duplicate-email
  400), login (success, invalid-credentials 401), refresh (success,
  invalid-token 401), 2fa/setup + 2fa/enable (success + failure 400),
  API key store/list/delete (success, failure, masked fields,
  not-found 404), billing performance-report/fees/invoices.
- No production code changes. Full suite verified green: 1161
  passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed. Coverage 91.98% -> 92.79%. ruff
  unchanged (22, pre-existing). mypy sgr/ unchanged (118,
  pre-existing).
